# WinFixer (2004-2008). Scareware: a pop-up and a fake scan "found" errors, then a nagging program demanded payment to fix them. A US court fined the company behind it in 2008.
# A quest (QUESTS.md): the trainee places the day's office supply orders, does one safely, then meets a "your computer is infected" page on a price-checking trip.
os windows
user Dana Okafor
about
  | WinFixer pop-ups and web pages claimed a free scan had found hundreds of errors and threats, and offered to fix them for a fee.
  | The "errors" were made up, and the program fixed nothing. It started with Windows and kept up the alerts until the victim paid. In 2008 a US court fined the company behind it.
  | WinFixer was not tied to one job; most victims met it on an ordinary web page. The office worker in this training is invented, to show how it reached people at work.
story
  | You are Dana Okafor, office coordinator at Northwind Traders. Marcus has asked you to place five supply orders today, all in before five o'clock.
  | It is mid-afternoon. You have placed 3 of the 5. Two to go.
  | The company card number and the supplier shop's sign-in are in two text files on the desktop. That is a bad habit, but it keeps this training quick.
quota 3 5 Supply orders placed today

# Dana's desk: the details she copies from (soft flags: careless, but only here to keep the training simple).
file Desktop/company-card.txt
  at 930 200
  | Northwind company card (training copy)
  | Card number: 4000 0012 3456 7899
  | Card PIN: 4417
file Desktop/shop-login.txt
  at 930 300
  | Brightline Office Supplies
  | User: dana.okafor
  | Password: Stapler-2026!

# The safe task: toner, from the supplier Northwind always uses.
page toner-done brightline-supplies.example/orders/confirmed
  title Brightline Office Supplies: order placed
  brand Brightline Office Supplies
  heading Order placed
  | Order BR-5521, 4 black toner cartridges, 168.00 paid by company card. Delivery on Thursday.
page toner brightline-supplies.example/orders/toner
  title Brightline Office Supplies: your order
  brand Brightline Office Supplies
  favorite
  heading Review your order
  | Ready to place, as Priya asked.
  section Order
  row Item = Black toner cartridge, for the 3rd floor printer
  row Quantity = 4
  row Price = 168.00
  row Pay with = Northwind company card ending 7899
  row Delivery = Thursday
  button Place order -> toner-done
mail mail-toner
  from Priya Shah <priya.shah@northwind.example>
  subject Toner for the 3rd floor printer (order 4 of 5)
  link toner
  | Hi Dana,
  |
  | The 3rd floor printer is nearly out of toner. Brightline have our usual cartridges in stock. The link goes straight to the order, ready to place.
  |
  | Priya

step Order 4 of 5
  look Mail: Priya's message with the supplier link
  | A message has come in from Priya, in Accounts, about toner. This one is real. Place the order the normal way, so you know what normal looks like.
notify mail Priya Shah
  | Toner for the 3rd floor printer (order 4 of 5)

step The supplier's own page
  look the address, then the item, the price and the card
  when visit toner
  | The email links to Brightline's own address, brightline-supplies.example, the shop Northwind always uses. Hover over a link before you click it, to check where it goes.
  | The page shows what Priya promised: the item, the quantity, the price. Check them, then place the order.
open toner

step Order 4 of 5 placed
  look the counter in the guide: 4 of 5
  when choose toner any
  | Placed. 4 of 5. The page did what the email said and nothing else. Marcus has just sent a message about the last order.
choose toner 1
quota +1

# The lure: a review site with a sponsored advert, then the "free scan" tab the advert opens.
page label-done brightline-supplies.example/orders/confirmed-label
  title Brightline Office Supplies: order placed
  brand Brightline Office Supplies
  heading Order placed
  | Order BR-5522, 1 Lumen LP-200 label printer, 124.00 paid by company card. Delivery on Friday.
page label-order brightline-supplies.example/orders/label-printer
  title Brightline Office Supplies: your order
  brand Brightline Office Supplies
  heading Review your order
  | Ready to place, as Marcus asked.
  section Order
  row Item = Lumen LP-200 label printer, for the post room
  row Quantity = 1
  row Price = 124.00
  row Pay with = Northwind company card ending 7899
  row Delivery = Friday
  button Place order -> label-done
page scan free-pc-scan.invalid/online-scan
  title Free online PC scan
  heading WARNING: your computer may be infected!
  | A free scan of your computer has found errors and threats.
  | Download WinFixer now to remove them.
  insecure
  section Scan results
  tone bad
  progress 100
  columns Problem | Found | Risk
  cells Registry errors | 98 | High
  cells Privacy risks | 19 | Medium
  cells Trojans | 3 | Critical
  button Download WinFixer
  button Cancel
page label-guide printerpicks.example/best-label-printers
  title PrinterPicks: best label printers 2026
  brand PrinterPicks
  heading Best label printers for small offices
  | We tested eight label printers for shipping and post-room use. Our favourite is below.
  section Our top pick
  row Model = Lumen LP-200
  row Print width = 100 mm
  row Typical price = from 119.00
  section Sponsored
  note Is your PC running slowly? Get a free scan in seconds.
  button Check today's price
mail mail-label
  from Marcus Lee <marcus.lee@northwind.example>
  subject Label printer for the post room: find a price
  link label-guide
  | Dana,
  |
  | The post room needs a label printer, and it is order 5. I have not had time to look. This site reviewed a good one: see what it costs, and we will order it.
  |
  | Marcus
notify mail Marcus Lee
  | Label printer for the post room: find a price

step A price check for Marcus
  look the link under Marcus's message, then the Sponsored advert
  when visit label-guide
  | Marcus's message is ordinary: a colleague you know, asking for a price. The link goes to printerpicks.example, a review site you have not used before. It looks fine, with a Sponsored advert on it.
  | Nothing is wrong with Marcus's email. It is the pages around the link to watch.
open label-guide

step A tab says your computer is infected
  look the "Not secure" address, the scan results and the buttons
  when choose label-guide 1
  | Pressing the price button opened a new tab, an advert and not a price. It claims a free scan has found 98 registry errors, 19 privacy risks and 3 trojans.
  | A web page cannot look inside your computer, so the numbers are made up to frighten you. Flag what looks wrong.
choose label-guide 1
open scan

step The download
  look the new file in Downloads
  when choose scan any
  | Either button starts the same download: the browser saves WinFixerSetup.exe in Downloads. You were looking for a printer price, not software, and an advert has just put a program on the computer.
choose scan 1
file Downloads/WinFixerSetup.exe
  program winfixer
  size 2097152
notify browser Download complete
  | WinFixerSetup.exe was saved in Downloads
open Downloads

# The program: an installer from an unknown publisher. Most victims ran it and allowed the changes.
view wf-setup wizard
  title WinFixer Setup
  app WinFixer Setup
  publisher Unknown Publisher
  page Install WinFixer
  icon program
  | WinFixer will find and repair problems on this computer. These extras are included.
  section Included offers
  check [x] Install the WinFixer toolbar
  check [x] Start WinFixer every time the computer starts
  check [x] Scan my computer for free when setup finishes
  note All three boxes are already ticked.
  button Install -> next primary
  button Cancel -> close
  page Setup complete
  icon shield-ok
  | WinFixer is installed. A scan will start now.
  button Finish -> done primary
view wf-pay message
  title WinFixer: payment (training copy)
  app WinFixer
  icon money
  | A card form would open here and ask for 49.95 USD. Nothing in this training asks for a real card.
  button OK -> close primary
view wf-scan scan
  title WinFixer: system scan (training copy)
  app WinFixer
  publisher Unknown Publisher
  page Scan results
  icon shield-bad
  heading 117 problems found
  | WinFixer scanned your computer and found these problems.
  section Scan results
  progress 100
  columns Problem | Count | Risk
  cells Registry errors | 98 | High
  cells Privacy risks | 19 | Medium
  cells Trojans | 3 | Critical
  note No real scan took place. The same numbers appear on every computer.
  button Fix all problems -> next primary
  button Close -> close
  page Register to fix
  icon money
  heading Register WinFixer to remove 117 problems
  | The free version can only find problems. To fix them you must buy the full version.
  section Price
  row Full version = 49.95 USD
  row Problems found = 117
  row Problems fixed = 0
  tone bad
  note Nothing was ever repaired. The alerts came back until the victim paid.
  button Buy full version -> view:wf-pay primary
  button Remind me later -> done
program winfixer WinFixerSetup.exe
  publisher none
  signed no
  prompt open-warning
  prompt elevation
  description WinFixer installer
  process WinFixer.exe
  cpu 9
  mem 42
  parent WinFixerSetup.exe
  command C:\Program Files\WinFixer\WinFixer.exe
  startup WinFixer C:\Program Files\WinFixer\WinFixer.exe
  location HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run
  view wf-setup

step The warning
  look Publisher "Unknown Publisher", Type "Application"
  when prompt winfixer
  | A page you did not ask for gave you a program, and the computer asks before it runs it: the publisher is unknown. Many people clicked Run anyway.
open Downloads/WinFixerSetup.exe

step Two questions, and boxes already ticked
  look the installer window: three ticked boxes, and the banners
  when run winfixer
  move Press “Install” in the installer window, as most people do. If another window covers it, click the installer first.
  | The computer asked twice: to run the file, and to allow changes to the system. Both questions say the publisher is unknown. The installer offers a toolbar, start-up with the computer and a free scan, all ticked in advance.
  | WinFixer.exe is already running and has added itself to start-up, before you pressed Install.
answer run
answer run
close files

step Setup is done
  look the installer's last page
  when page wf-setup 2
  | The installer reports success. The next thing it does is the scan it promised.
press wf-setup next

step A scan that finds everything
  look the WinFixer scan: 117 problems, and the note under the table
  when done wf-setup
  | WinFixer "scans" the computer and finds 117 problems, the same on every computer. The scan never looked at your files.
show wf-scan
notify settings Your PC is at risk!
  | 117 errors found. Click to fix now. (Fake: no scan took place.)

step Fixing costs money
  look the price page: "Buy full version" and "Remind me later"
  when page wf-scan 2
  move Press “Remind me later” to close the WinFixer window, and get back to the order.
  | Fix all problems leads to a price: 49.95 USD. Nothing is repaired until you pay, and nothing was ever broken.
  | WinFixer.exe keeps running and starts with the computer, so the alerts keep coming.
press wf-scan next

# The payoff: the alerts return while Dana finishes the last order.

step The reminders return
  look the banner and Marcus's new message
  when done wf-scan
  move Open Marcus's message and follow its link to the order.
  | You pressed “Remind me later”, and it did not take long. WinFixer is still running, so its banner is back on the screen.
  | Marcus has found the printer at Brightline, the shop you trust. Open his message to finish the last order.
mail mail-order
  from Marcus Lee <marcus.lee@northwind.example>
  subject Forget the review site: order the Lumen from Brightline
  link label-order
  | Dana,
  |
  | Brightline have the Lumen LP-200 at 124.00, so order it there. The link goes straight to the order.
  |
  | Marcus
notify settings Your PC is at risk!
  | WinFixer: 117 problems still found. Register now to remove them.
notify mail Marcus Lee
  | Forget the review site: order the Lumen from Brightline

step The last order
  look the address, then the item, the price and the card
  when visit label-order
  | The same shop and the same page you used for the toner. The alerts are a distraction, not part of the order. Check it, then place it.
open label-order

step Order 5 of 5, or so Dana thinks
  look the counter: the shift is done, and the banner again
  when choose label-order any
  | Every order is placed, and the computer still works. But WinFixer.exe is still running, and the alerts will keep coming. Press Next to see what it was.
choose label-order 1
quota +1
notify settings Your PC is at risk!
  | WinFixer: register now. Your computer is not protected.

step What WinFixer was
  look Task Manager: WinFixer.exe, still running
  | WinFixer was never a scanner. It started from an advert, invented 117 problems, charged 49.95 USD to fix them and fixed nothing. Paying meant a card number sent to the people behind it.
  | Removing it means taking it out of the start-up list and uninstalling it, using security software you already trust.
attack scareware
  | 98 registry errors
  | 19 privacy risks
  | 3 trojans
  | pay 49.95 USD
  | 0 problems fixed
open taskmanager
block 203.0.113.60 443

flag hard section scan 1
  | A web page cannot scan your computer. These numbers are made up to frighten you.
flag hard choice scan 1
  | An advert pushing you to download software you were not looking for.
flag hard file Downloads/WinFixerSetup.exe
  | A program that arrived from an advert, not from the maker of your security software.
flag hard dialog open-warning winfixer
  | Publisher: Unknown. A price page does not need to run a program on your computer.
flag hard dialog elevation winfixer
  | A cleaner from an advert asking to change the computer, with an unknown publisher.
flag hard process WinFixer.exe
  | WinFixer keeps running in the background, so the alerts keep coming.
flag hard startup WinFixer
  | It added itself to the programs that start with the computer, whatever the ticked box says.
flag soft file Desktop/company-card.txt
  | A card number and PIN in a text file on the desktop: any program that runs can read them. Use a password manager.
flag soft file Desktop/shop-login.txt
  | A shop password in a text file on the desktop. Use a password manager.

lesson
  | A web page cannot scan your computer. Alarming numbers with a price attached mean scareware: close the tab.
  | Do not run a program an advert gave you. Untick pre-ticked extras, and use the security software that came with your system.
  | If a program like this is already on the computer, remove it through the list of installed apps, and do not pay to "fix" what it invented.
